From 16e9d534b2a91773eae0546338d80027a17769b1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Geonmo Ryu <geonmo@kisti.re.kr>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 10:18:14 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] xrootd: answer space queries with the configured capacity

Motivation:
The xrootd door doesn't support kXR_Qspace queries. As a result,
`xrdfs spaceinfo` fails and `df` on a directory mounted with xrootdfs
shows a size of zero, so plain `df` hides the mount, while the NFS door
reports a size of 1 EiB for the same instance.

Modification:
Handle kXR_Qspace in XrootdRedirectHandler, reporting the capacity
selected by the new xrootd.capacity.source and
xrootd.capacity.reservation properties (defaulting to
dcache.capacity.source and dcache.capacity.reservation) in the format of
xrootd's oss plugin:

- namespace (default): a fixed size of 1 EiB, all of which is free
- pools: the total and free space summed over all online pools
- reservation: the configured space reservation or, if none is
  configured, the one given by the WriteToken directory tag of the
  queried path, as the FTP door does for SITE USAGE

The queried path must exist and be accessible by the user. Space
reservations are looked up through the existing ReservationCaches space
lookup cache, for which a space manager cell stub is added to the door.

Result:
xrootd clients see a capacity for dCache, consistent with the NFS door:
by default, `xrdfs spaceinfo` succeeds and `df` on an xrootdfs mount
shows 1 EiB instead of hiding the mount. Sites can report the capacity
of the pools or of a space reservation instead.

