+### Space usage queries
+
+The door answers space queries (`kXR_Qspace`), e.g. from `xrdfs spaceinfo`
+or `df` on a directory mounted with `xrootdfs`, in the same format as
+xrootd's oss plugin. The reported capacity is selected by
+`xrootd.capacity.source`, which defaults to `dcache.capacity.source`:
+
+| Value | Reported size | Reported free space |
+|---|---|---|
+| `namespace` (default) | 1 EiB | 1 EiB |
+| `pools` | Sum of the total space of all online pools | Sum of the free and removable space of those pools |
+| `reservation` | Size of the space reservation | Space neither used nor allocated in the reservation |
+
+With `reservation`, the space reservation is given by
+`xrootd.capacity.reservation` or, if that is empty, by the `WriteToken`
+directory tag of the queried path. For paths without a `WriteToken` tag
+the query then fails. For example:
+
+```ini
+xrootd.capacity.source = reservation
+```
+
+```console-user
+xrdfs door.example.org spaceinfo /data/cms
+|Path:               /data/cms
+|Total:              1099511627776
+|Free:               274877906944
+|Used:               824633720832
+|Largest free chunk: 274877906944
+```
+
+The queried path must exist and be accessible by the user.
+
